   "id": "lightfoot",
   "title": "Operation Lightfoot: the break-in",
   "time": "Night, 23-24 Oct",
   "narrative": "At 21:40 on 23 October about nine hundred guns opened up, and XXX Corps infantry walked west on a front of some twenty-six kilometres toward the Oxalic Line. Montgomery wanted two corridors cut through the mines in the north so that X Corps tanks could pass through. The infantry got into the outpost zone, but clearing lanes in the dark took far longer than planned, and in the south the diversion by XIII Corps made little headway.",
