  {
   "id": "stuck",
   "title": "The armour is held at the minefields",
   "time": "24 Oct",
   "narrative": "Dawn showed the Axis line bent but unbroken. General Stumme, driving forward to see for himself, died of a heart attack, and von Thoma took temporary command. Allied armour stayed bottled up at the Oxalic Line while engineers lifted mines. At dusk the 15th Panzer and Littorio divisions came out of the Kidney depression, and the first big tank action of the battle began. Over a hundred tanks were involved and about half were lost by nightfall, without changing the line.",
