  {
   "id": "rommel-shifts",
   "title": "Rommel pulls his armour north",
   "time": "26-28 Oct",
   "narrative": "Convinced the main blow would fall in the north, Rommel ordered counter-attacks on Point 29 and Hill 28, and moved the 21st Panzer Division, part of the Ariete and half the southern artillery up to join the 15th Panzer and Littorio. With so little petrol, the move could not be reversed. On 28 October the two panzer divisions struck X Corps, but artillery and air attack broke up the assembly. It was Rommel's last attempt to seize the initiative.",
