   "title": "The 9th Armoured Brigade charges the guns",
   "time": "06:15, 2 Nov",
   "narrative": "At 06:15, half an hour before dawn, the brigade set off behind a creeping barrage with 94 of its 132 tanks still running. German and Italian anti-tank guns, among them 24 of the 88 mm flak guns, fired at tanks outlined by the rising sun. About 35 guns were destroyed in thirty minutes, but only 24 tanks were left running and 230 of 400 men were killed, wounded or captured. The gap for 1st Armoured was not yet open.",
