   "title": "The Axis front collapses",
   "time": "4 Nov",
   "narrative": "On 4 November 1st and 7th Armoured Divisions swung north and the New Zealanders headed west along desert tracks. The Ariete fought to the end against British tanks that had come round its open flank, while the Littorio and Trieste were also destroyed, and the unmotorised Italian infantry were left behind. By early afternoon Rommel judged his front broken, with a hole 19 kilometres wide, and radioed Hitler for leave to fall back on Fuka.",
